      "verification": "not_recorded",
      "verification_note": "KRS 141.020 confirms the flat rates by year. It does not state the standard deduction. The 2018 Form 740 packet (https://revenue.ky.gov/Forms/740%20Packet.pdf, sha256 fea24e4fbbb57e300dc0de0498ce49f059c9cc38833cf5876d51195657bf99a5, retrieved 2026-11-10) states the standard deduction is $2,530. That is the held 2018 deduction. The 2019 Form 740 packet (https://revenue.ky.gov/Forms/2019%20740%20Instruction%20Packet.pdf, sha256 1afca706b3027bb1ebccb02d8e7e735691d2d2c7c6ba5d502387265ca9d87f86, retrieved 2026-11-10) states the standard deduction is $2,590. The 2020 Form 740 packet (https://revenue.ky.gov/Forms/740%20Instructions%20Packet%205.7.21.pdf, sha256 51f3c2dfa4decd141d528348cde013f9de10231c39a0ea91badb3dcaea235304, retrieved 2026-11-10) states the standard deduction is $2,650. The 2021 Form 740 packet (https://revenue.ky.gov/Forms/Form%20740%20Packet%20Instructions-2021.pdf, sha256 714b561d98e16484df873611e58558d478d136785a4fbd9e1f3fc49de940f25f, retrieved 2026-11-10) states the standard deduction is $2,690. The 2022 Form 740 packet instructions (https://revenue.ky.gov/Forms/740%20Packet%20Instructions%205-9-23.pdf, sha256 fa4d83d689acf2a86b439cce152ca3020b0ee822f505f03e16fe8f7e24b4669a, retrieved 2026-11-10) state the standard deduction is $2,770. The 2023 Form 740 packet instructions (https://revenue.ky.gov/Forms/740%20Packet%20Instructions%202023.pdf, sha256 cd3242f0e358d0bad1bda6c8e2961327c142ccc651fc82b5ea99ece2ea506a8b, retrieved 2026-11-10) state the standard deduction is $2,980. The 2024 e-file handbook (https://revenue.ky.gov/Documents/TY2024%20E-File%20HandBook%20Publication%201345_v1.0.pdf, sha256 ff1518fdfb27eeac42f780fef0a727dc4d7d359866da6cf0b60dee5eabca850a, retrieved 2026-11-10) states the standard deduction increased from $2,980 to $3,160 for tax year 2024, which cross-checks the 2023 amount and is the held 2024 deduction. The 2025 Form 740 packet (https://revenue.ky.gov/Forms/740%20Packet%20Instructions.pdf, sha256 cdb8e571c09f306961d5cb62154f8b57bd67f6ee50376b443647376b5667f421, retrieved 2026-11-10) states a 4% rate and a $3,270 standard deduction. The 2026 withholding formula (https://revenue.ky.gov/Forms/2026%20Withholding%20Formula.pdf, sha256 3876018d7019cf2b8ffae40554376ef2e6900809221517c26d8e71e025f5e439, retrieved 2026-11-10) states a 3.5% rate and a $3,360 standard deduction. The September 4, 2025 DOR announcement (https://revenue.ky.gov/News/Pages/Kentucky-DOR-Announces-2026-Standard-Deduction.aspx, sha256 f058b78a07a43e541838fd35a2b991f90e70a1d50e7cd4fcaf1ac1d994875416, retrieved 2026-11-10) states the 2026 standard deduction is $3,360.",
